@startuml
title Diagrama de secuencia — Turno y cierre de caja

autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "ENCARGADO / ADMINISTRADOR" as User
participant "Frontend web" as Frontend
participant "Shifts API" as ShiftsApi
participant "Cash Closing API" as ClosingApi
participant "Application\n(Shifts / Cash Closing)" as App
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== Inicio / activación de turno ==

User -> Frontend : iniciar / activar turno
Frontend -> ShiftsApi : PATCH /shifts/{id}/start
ShiftsApi -> App : StartShift(command)
App -> DB : obtener Shift + CashSession
App -> DB : actualizar Shift=ACTIVE
App --> ShiftsApi : turno activo
ShiftsApi --> Frontend : 200 OK
Frontend --> User : mostrar turno activo

== Continuidad / traspaso ==

opt finalizar turno con traspaso
  User -> Frontend : finalizar turno
  Frontend -> ShiftsApi : PATCH /shifts/{id}/complete
  ShiftsApi -> App : CompleteShift(command)
  App -> DB : registrar handover amounts + note
  App -> DB : actualizar Shift=COMPLETED
  App --> ShiftsApi : turno completado
  ShiftsApi --> Frontend : 200 OK
  Frontend --> User : mostrar turno completado
end

== Cierre final de caja ==

User -> Frontend : preparar cierre
Frontend -> ClosingApi : GET /cash-closings/summary?cashSessionId=...
ClosingApi -> App : BuildClosingSummary(query)
App -> DB : consultar ventas por canal
App -> DB : consultar gastos por fuente
App -> DB : consultar sesión y turnos
App --> ClosingApi : expected cash + resumen
ClosingApi --> Frontend : 200 OK
Frontend --> User : mostrar resumen esperado

User -> Frontend : registrar cierre
Frontend -> ClosingApi : POST /cash-closings
ClosingApi -> App : RegisterCashClosing(command)
App -> DB : guardar CashClosing
App -> DB : actualizar CashSession=CLOSED
App --> ClosingApi : cierre registrado
ClosingApi --> Frontend : 201 Created
Frontend --> User : mostrar cierre guardado

note bottom
Fratelli opera con dos turnos, una sola caja y un único cierre final.
El cierre pertenece a la sesión de caja, no a un turno individual.
end note

@enduml
